<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>R is the region given by <m>{3x + 8y \le 30}</m>, <m>{x + 6y \gt 4}</m>, <m>{x \ge 1}</m>, <m>x \ge 0</m> and <m>y \ge 0</m>.</p><p>(a) Give a point of R whose coordinates are whole numbers: ( <fillin characters="4" name="ans1"/> , <fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/> )  </p><div/><p>(b) Give a point of R with whole-number coordinates that lies on the line <m>{3x + 8y = 30}</m>: ( <fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/> , <fillin characters="4" name="ans4"/> )  </p><div/><p>There is more than one right answer.</p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Test a point in every inequality. For example <m>({1}, {1})</m> is in R: <m>{3} \times {1} + {8} \times {1} = {11} \le {30}</m>, <m>{1} \times {1} + {6} \times {1} = {7} \gt {4}</m>, and it satisfies <m>{x \ge 1}</m>. R has <m>{19}</m> whole-number points in all.</p><p>(b) The line <m>{3x + 8y = 30}</m> is solid, so its points can be in R. Whole-number points of R on it: <m>{\left[ \left[ 2 , 3 \right] , \left[ 10 , 0 \right] \right]}</m>. Points on the dashed line <m>{1}x + {6}y = {4}</m> are not in R.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>3</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>